e's a lot of issues going on  and we're not addressing them the  executive director of youth mental  health canada says the pandemic has made  problems of mental health youth suicide  and youth violence more severe and not  enough is being done to support kids we  don't respond with immediacy or efficacy  when young people are in crisis in a  health crisis we put people on a wait  list statistics show young racialized  men are particularly vulnerable we  really need to be attending to the way  kids get along with each other bullying  rates are really high in canada they're  among the highest of economically  advanced countries in the world canada's  research chair on school-based violence  prevention says schools are still not  doing enough to tackle the country's  bullying problem  after two years of collective trauma the  need for social and emotional  developmental support is perhaps needed  more now than ever before heather yorks  west global news calgary  shanghai confirms its first deaths  linked to china's biggest covet outbreak  since the virus was first discovered all  three people were elderly and had  underlying health conditions and were  not vaccinated shanghai china's  financial hub is now entering another  round of mass testing to help curb the  spread most of the city's 25 million  residents are also being confined to  their homes for a third straight week  despite the easing of other public  health measures still ahead violent  clashes in sweden what sparked the  chaotic demonstrations next  [Music]  at least 40 people have been injured in  riots that spread throughout sweden over  the easter weekend protesters are angry  a danish far-right politician with  swedish roots burned a koran during a  tour of the country 20 police vehicles  have been damaged or destroyed and more  than two dozen people arrested police  are calling the riots extremely serious  crimes against society and they believe  some protesters might have links to  criminal gangs that