nd then you try to  pull it out and your foot comes out but  not the boot kind of the same thing on a  grander scale it all started in march  when the ever forward missed a turn and  ran aground in shallow water for 36 days  she was beached they tried pushing and  pulling with tugboats they tried  dredging around the hull  it started to feel like the ever forward  might be stuck forever  it's not unlike what happened to the  ever given a sister ship of the ever  forward that became wedged in the suez  canal last year it took six days and a  lot of digging to set her free  weeks after getting stuck the ever  forward needed some forward thinking  crews made the risky decision to remove  about 500 of her 5 000 containers at sea  to lighten the load  high hopes and high tide set the boat  back afloat they have to survey the  vessel to determine the amount of damage  done to it it's been sitting on the  bottom for five weeks even if the vessel  is found to be in ship shape the fate of  her containers is now about as clear as  the mud she was stuck in  maritime law allows the shipping company  to charge its customers for some of the  cost of saving the vessel  the ever forward may be free  her cargo could stay stuck in the courts  for months  jackson prosko global news washington  and that is global national for this  monday night i'm chris galas and we'll  leave you tonight with some wildlife  wrestling  oh oh now they're both in there it's  wrestlemania  young black bears emerged from  hibernation to duke it out in a bc  backyard trampoline luckily for the  owners it remained undamaged once the  two animals bounced off probably to  continue their cage match somewhere else  hope you enjoyed that thanks very much  for watching donna friesen we'll be back  with you tomorrow hope you have a great  evening  [Applause]  [Music]
 

